            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor raised the issue of whether a statutory penalty that functions like a tax should be treated as a tax."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7f9c90f69995f5bc79e01c3baa3066c820a42f4edeaa1e8cfdf61a7635165175",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7f9c90f69995-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 50,
              "start": 50
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked whether Congress\u2019s decision not to label the payment as a tax changes its constitutional analysis."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7f9c90f69995f5bc79e01c3baa3066c820a42f4edeaa1e8cfdf61a7635165175",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7f9c90f69995-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 59,
              "start": 59
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg compared the mandate to the Social Security system, noting that Congress used a tax to fund a universal program."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7f9c90f69995f5bc79e01c3baa3066c820a42f4edeaa1e8cfdf61a7635165175",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7f9c90f69995-0003-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 60,
              "start": 60
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor inquired whether an exemption could be created so that those who already have insurance would not pay the shared responsibility payment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7f9c90f69995f5bc79e01c3baa3066c820a42f4edeaa1e8cfdf61a7635165175",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7f9c90f69995-0003-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 62,
              "start": 62
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer focused the discussion on the Commerce Clause, setting aside Due Process considerations."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7f9c90f69995f5bc79e01c3baa3066c820a42f4edeaa1e8cfdf61a7635165175",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7f9c90f69995-0003-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 70,
              "start": 70
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan reiterated the theory that people are in the health\u2011care market because they can become sick and need care."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7f9c90f69995f5bc79e01c3baa3066c820a42f4edeaa1e8cfdf61a7635165175",
            "evidence_ids": [
